<item><title>AMEA Power signs $650m Egypt wind deals and first turbine factory contracts</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/eg/amea-power-signs-650m-egypt-wind-deals-and-first-turbine-22fd2b/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/eg/amea-power-signs-650m-egypt-wind-deals-and-first-turbine-22fd2b/</guid><category>Egypt</category><description>The contracts cover a 500 MW wind farm at Ras Shukeir on the Red Sea and a turbine factory in the Suez Canal Economic Zone with annual capacity of 3 GW.</description><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:13:02 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/eg.jpg" length="31241" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/eg.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Egypt takes top spot for EU apple exports outside the bloc</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/eg/egypt-takes-top-spot-for-eu-apple-exports-outside-the-bloc-92759b/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/eg/egypt-takes-top-spot-for-eu-apple-exports-outside-the-bloc-92759b/</guid><category>Egypt</category><description>EU shipments rose 32% to 190,000 tonnes in 2025/26, putting Egypt ahead of the United Kingdom by about 36,000 tonnes.</description><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 11:59:33 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/eg.jpg" length="31241" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/eg.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
